# Reactant complex for K + H2O2 (2 waters, Grotthuss relay) -> KP
# (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8 item 1). Geometry confirmed by direct connectivity
# analysis 2026-09-09 (bond distances, not assumed from the folder name):
# intact ketone C129=O130 (1.218 A), intact H2O2 (H135-O136-O137-H138,
# O-O 1.46 A), two intact waters (O132: H131,H139; O134: H133,H140) -- no
# BnOH, no HOO-, charge 0. See ../../README.md-equivalent note in this
# folder's parent for how this superseded catHO2(-)+BnOH/, which turned out
# to be a different, unidentified three-body system
# (../../K+peroxide+BnOH_bridged_UNIDENTIFIED/).
#
# Corrected from the version orca_stuff carried, 2026-09-09:
#
# 1. ALPB(Water) -> ddCOSMO(Water). QM/XTB's ALPB only solvates the QM2 (xtb)
#    layer, NOT the QM1 (r2SCAN-3c) region where the actual chemistry is --
#    ORCA 6.1 manual, Multiscale Simulations: "If the ALPB model or CPCM-X
#    are requested [within QM/XTB], the solvation effect is just included
#    in the calculation for the large QM2 system." The manual's fix for that
#    is "C-PCM or ddCOSMO... with the default C-PCM/B scheme" -- but plain
#    CPCM itself is NOT implemented for QM/XTB (tried it first: ORCA aborts
#    at input-check with "CPCM or SMD requested together with QM/XTB method.
#    This is not implemented. Provide respective ALPB, ddCOSMO or CPCMX
#    keyword instead."). ddCOSMO is the one of those three that still gets
#    the C-PCM/B-style propagation: cavity charges computed once on the
#    full QM2 system, then reused as point charges feeding the QM1
#    calculation too -- the only one of the three that actually solvates the
#    reactive region itself, not just the xtb scaffold. Matters here
#    specifically because the TS moves charge across four centres
#    (H2O2 -> water2 -> water1 -> ketone O) in a polar relay. Mechanism is
#    single-pass (QM2's own solvation computed once, not iterated to
#    self-consistency with QM1's density) -- the manual doesn't specify
#    iteration either way, but says "once this calculation finishes...
#    used as... subsequent", i.e. sequential.
#
# 2. nprocs 12 / maxcore 2200 -> nprocs 8 / maxcore 4000: homelab-benchmarked
#    (COMPUTATIONAL.md Conventions, 2026-09-09) -- 8 physical P-cores beat
#    16/24 ranks on this machine's hybrid P/E chip for jobs this size.
#
# 3. Added Recalc_Hess 50, 2026-09-09, after a first attempt (bare
#    Calc_Hess true, no refresh -- attempt1_no_recalc/) converged steadily
#    through cycle ~111 then started regressing by cycle 131 (RMS/MAX
#    gradient both got WORSE, not better) -- the same RFO-Hessian-drift
#    signature the TS searches showed, milder here since a plain
#    minimization's BFGS/RFO update is more forgiving than TS eigenvector-
#    following. 50, not the TS's 10: minimizations don't need refreshing as
#    often, and this system's full Hessian recompute costs real wall time.
#    Restarted from attempt 1's cycle-131 geometry
#    (attempt1_no_recalc/job_cycle131.xyz), not from scratch.
#
# 4. QM region enlarged from 12 to 20 atoms, 2026-09-19, to match the TS: added
#    the two alpha-carbons (C121, C125) with their CH2 hydrogens and the two
#    beta-ether oxygens (O65, O62). Without them the QM1 carbonyl was capped by
#    two link H -- i.e. H2C=O, an aldehyde-like electrophile -- whereas the TS
#    models the real 1,3-dialkoxy ketone; reactant and TS must share the QM
#    region for a barrier to mean anything. The 12-atom version is kept in
#    attempt1_qm12/. Also added AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF (the tier convention)
#    and %output jsonpropfile true end (orca_io/OPI reads the property JSON).

! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137 138 139}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 50
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
